<procedure><preliminaryRqmts><reqCondGroup><reqCondDm><reqCond>The used filler-breather cap is removed.</reqCond><dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="VH15" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="10" subSystemCode="0" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="00" disassyCode="04" disassyCodeVariant="A" infoCode="520" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="A"/></dmRefIdent></dmRef></reqCondDm></reqCondGroup><reqSupportEquips><noSupportEquips/></reqSupportEquips><reqSupplies><supplyDescrGroup><supplyDescr id="sup-0001"><name>Lint-free cloth</name><supplyRef supplyNumber="LINT-FREE-CLOTH" supplyNumberType="sp05"/><reqQuantity>As required</reqQuantity></supplyDescr></supplyDescrGroup></reqSupplies><reqSpares><spareDescrGroup><spareDescr id="spa-0001"><name>Filler-breather cap, 10 micrometers</name><identNumber><manufacturerCode>VH000</manufacturerCode><partAndSerialNumber><partNumber>VH15-1004</partNumber></partAndSerialNumber></identNumber><reqQuantity>1</reqQuantity></spareDescr></spareDescrGroup></reqSpares><reqSafety><safetyRqmts><caution><warningAndCautionPara>Do not let dirt into the reservoir. Dirt in the hydraulic oil can cause damage to the pump and the valves.</warningAndCautionPara></caution></safetyRqmts></reqSafety></preliminaryRqmts><mainProcedure><proceduralStep><para>Make sure that the part number on the new filler-breather cap is VH15-1004.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Remove the cloth from the filler opening.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Make sure that the filler strainer is in the cap.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Install the filler-breather cap. Turn it clockwise until it is tight by hand. Do not use tools.</para></proceduralStep></mainProcedure><closeRqmts><reqCondGroup><reqCondNoRef><reqCond>The filler-breather cap is installed.</reqCond></reqCondNoRef></reqCondGroup></closeRqmts></procedure>
